Error [E0068]: This callable uses the retired result-arrow shape.
  --> tests/ui/crypto_secret_nested_provenance.jet:15:45
    |
 15 | fn accept_callback(value: fn(crypto.Secret) => crypto.Secret) {}
    |                                             ^^
 Why: a return type sits after the parameter list, and `->` introduces the body; an effect ceiling follows the return type
 Fix: write `fn name(...) Type -> body`, or `fn name(...) Type -[Effects]> { … }`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0068

Error [E0070]: this uses a retired arrow spelling
  --> tests/ui/crypto_secret_nested_provenance.jet:31:40
    |
 31 |     callback :: (value: crypto.Secret) => value
    |                                        ^^
 Why: callables, arms, and lambdas use one arrow: `->`
 Fix: replace `:>` or `=>` with `->`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0070

Error [E1004]: `core.crypto` exposes `Secret`, but not in this position
  --> tests/ui/crypto_secret_nested_provenance.jet:21:32
    |
 21 |     tagged :: #Reviewed crypto.Secret.from_text("tagged")
    |                                ^^^^^^
 Why: standard library modules expose a fixed set of public items, each reachable only where its surface declares
 Fix: import it directly with `use core.crypto.[Secret]`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1004

Error [E0119]: there's no type called `crypto.Secret`
  --> tests/ui/crypto_secret_nested_provenance.jet:31:25
    |
 31 |     callback :: (value: crypto.Secret) => value
    |                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: the types are `Int`, `Float`, `Bool`, and `String` (plus types you define)
 Fix: check the spelling, or define the struct or enum first
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0119

Error [E0721]: a `Reviewed` value is denied at `print`
  --> tests/ui/crypto_secret_nested_provenance.jet:23:5
    |
 23 |     print("{tagged}")
    |     ^^^^^
 Why: the declaration for `Reviewed` denies `Log`, which covers this destination
 Fix: remove the destination use, or pass the value through a matching `#Scrub(Reviewed)` function
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0721
